<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Gaia Belardinelli</title>
  <style>
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: #111315;
      color: #eaece9;
      font: 17px/1.7 Arial, sans-serif;
    }
    main { max-width: 860px; margin: auto; padding: 80px 28px; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 16px; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 80px 0 24px; }
    h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; }
    p { color: #b9beba; }
    a { color: #a6d5c0; }
    .intro { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 48px; }
    .intro img { width: 190px; height: 190px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 50%; }
    .role { color: #a6d5c0; }
    .item { border-top: 1px solid #363b39; padding: 22px 0; }
    .item p { margin: 0; }
    @media (max-width: 650px) {
      .intro { flex-direction: column-reverse; align-items: flex-start; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <div class="intro">
      <div>
        <h1>Gaia Belardinelli</h1>
        <p class="role">Postdoctoral Fellow · Technical University of Denmark</p>
        <p>I work on formal models of reasoning and rationality in multi-agent and epistemic settings. My research in logic explores how idealized models of reasoning relate to human social cognition.</p>
      </div>
      <img src="gaia.jpg" alt="Portrait of Gaia Belardinelli">
    </div>

    <h2>Research</h2>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Attention and awareness</h3>
      <p>How do attention and awareness affect what agents learn, believe, and infer?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Implicit cognition</h3>
      <p>I develop logical models of reasoning that account for explicit and implicit cognitive phenomena.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Models and methodology</h3>
      <p>Why can abstract mathematical models illuminate the world even when they leave so much out?</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Recent news</h2>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Advances in Modal Logic 2026</h3>
      <p>“Belief Contraction in Dynamic Epistemic Logic,” joint work with Snow Zhang, was accepted.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Nordic Logic Summer School 2026</h3>
      <p>I taught a course on formal models of attention.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>ESSLLI 2026</h3>
      <p>Snow Zhang and I taught a course on awareness modeling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Cal Poly Pomona</h3>
      <p>I gave an invited talk on logic in AI at the AI Fair and Hackathon.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Add Gaia’s email address and links to her CV, publications, and profiles here.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
